.claude/settings.local.json

# Ensure these files are tracked
!CLAUDE.md
!AGENTS.md

# Plans and their result ledgers ARE tracked. The plan is the master copy of the test
# content, and the ledger maps plan ids to Jira issues — a colleague working from a stale
# or absent ledger is what used to make a push create duplicates. Tracking them makes the
# plan reviewable in a PR and gives the work a backup.
#
# Note this repo is PUBLIC, so anything written into a plan step is world-readable and
# permanent. Keep client-confidential detail out of plan text, or move plans/ into a
# private repo checked out at this path.
#
# The jira-actions file is regenerated by every push and consumed immediately — pure churn.
.claude/qa/plans/*.jira-actions.json
